 // D-SHAPE-CLI1 / D-CLIFLAG1: the typed entry `fn run(args: T)` over a `#CLI`
-// struct `T`. The compiler appends `fn __jet_cli_run()`, which builds the
-// D-ARGS1 spec of `T` with the `core.args` `__cli_*` helpers, parses
-// `process.argv()` and then calls `run` (or, when `T` declares commands, the
-// selected command). The driver picks `__jet_cli_run` as the entry of such a
+// struct `T`. The compiler appends `fn __jet_cli_run()`, which parses
+// `process.argv()` against the D-ARGS1 spec of `T` and then calls `run` (or,
+// when `T` declares commands, the selected command). When `T` declares no
+// commands the entry calls `fn __jet_cli_parse() -> T`, a parser written for
+// exactly the inputs of `T` (sema_cli_entry_direct): help and error texts are
+// literals, and only an input of a kind links its check (the Float parser only
+// for a Float input).
+// A `T` with commands decodes its spec from a compact table written here
+// (`core.args` `__cli_spec`). The driver picks `__jet_cli_run` as the entry of such a
